From: GlassGlide contributors
Subject: [PATCH] WPEPlatform: do not link the unused Wayland EGL wrapper

The Wayland platform does not call wl_egl_window functions. Keep the Wayland
client and server libraries, but do not add wayland-egl through the generic
FindWayland result. The webOS SDK provides only a non-functional link stub,
which must not become a runtime dependency.

--- a/Source/WebKit/WPEPlatform/wpe/wayland/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/Source/WebKit/WPEPlatform/wpe/wayland/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -50,9 +50,11 @@ set(WPEPlatformWayland_SYSTEM_INCLUDE_DIRECTORIES
     ${WPEPlatform_SYSTEM_INCLUDE_DIRECTORIES}
 )
 
+set(WPEPlatformWayland_WAYLAND_LIBRARIES ${WAYLAND_LIBRARIES})
+list(REMOVE_ITEM WPEPlatformWayland_WAYLAND_LIBRARIES wayland-egl)
 set(WPEPlatformWayland_LIBRARIES
     GLib::GioUnix
-    ${WAYLAND_LIBRARIES}
+    ${WPEPlatformWayland_WAYLAND_LIBRARIES}
     ${WPEPlatform_LIBRARIES}
 )
 
